  <div class="info-box">
    <strong>Employer contribution:</strong> If you are employed, your employer contributes roughly half the premium, up to a maximum of approximately €421/month in 2026 (half the average GKV contribution at the Beitragsbemessungsgrenze). So a €400/month premium effectively costs you around €200/month out of pocket.
  </div>

  <p>For self-employed people, there is no employer contribution, so you pay the full premium. However, even at full cost, PKV is often cheaper than GKV for freelancers, because GKV charges 14.6% + a supplementary rate (typically 1.5-2%) on your entire income with no employer sharing it.</p>

  <p>Full breakdown: <a href="/guide/costs-and-contributions">PKV costs and contributions in 2026</a>.</p>

